  "final": "`DocumentService.archive` in `src/service.ts` now enforces the authorization rules. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes, and so does my new `checks/authz.cjs`.\n\n- **Visibility:** a document that is missing, deleted or in another tenant throws `Error('not found')` for every role, including admin.\n- **Permission:** an admin can archive any visible document. An editor can archive only documents they own. A viewer can never archive. Anyone else, including an unrecognised role, gets `Error('forbidden')`.\n- **Order of checks:** visibility is checked first, then permission, then the already-archived case. Repeating archive on an archived document does nothing for an authorized actor, but an unauthorized actor still gets `forbidden`.\n- **Success:** the existing `repository.archive` sets `archived` to true and appends `{actor: actor.user, document: id}` to the audit list.\n- **Failures:** every check runs before anything is written, so a failed call leaves all documents and the audit list unchanged.\n\nI didn't change any public interfaces. `checks/authz.cjs` covers the not-found cases, forbidden for viewers and non-owner editors, the permission check on already-archived documents, successful archives with their audit entries, and the no-op repeat. It also confirms nothing changed after the failures.",
